      },
      "text": "Figure 2: Comparison of Accuracy and Numerical Stability for HRBF and MHRBF: The errors (function, f , and its first derivatives, f x and f y ) and condition number computed in double precision for GA kernel, as functions of shape parameter ε , with polynomial degree of 6 and n = 4 for MHRBF.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.10527385616083969,
        "y0": 0.8096865386214351,
        "x1": 0.8948235776345763,
        "y1": 0.8690767202366105
      },
      "text": "The results in Figure 2 reveal significant accuracy improvements with MHRBF compared to HRBF. Since the error trends for ∇ f closely follow that of f , the subsequent analysis focuses primarily on the function interpolation. Figure 2a demonstrates that the MHRBF achieves low error over a large range of ε values, with the error ∼ 10 − 14 for all ε ≳ 0 . 5, despite the fact that the condition number of the MHRBF being",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
